      "id": "claim_64be05bdb9e14654b487ffcebceadf3a",
      "statement": "A Claim is an atomic, independently verifiable factual proposition about the system, backed by one or more evidence resources that jointly support it, where atomic means one coherent falsifiable idea rather than one symbol or source line; the shared CLAIMS_SUBSTANCE_GUIDANCE standard codifies this materiality test so it stays consistent across init, update, migration, and tool descriptions.",
